steps_to_reproduce:
1) Create a batched generation request (Go SDK) that includes two tool calls in sequence: recordEvent() -> sendWebhook().
2) Attach per-call idempotency tokens (X-Idempotency-Tool) to each function call payload.
3) Configure client to use the default retry coordinator with aggressive backoff (max retries 3).
4) Induce a transient network hiccup between orchestrator and serving runtime (iptables DROP for ~250ms) while a batch is being streamed.
5) Observe downstream systems (DB webhook consumer) for ordering and duplicate writes.

Minimal example (Go-like pseudocode):

client.GenerateBatch(ctx, batchRequest{
  sessions: [{
    prompt: "...",
    tools: [
      {name: "recordEvent", idempotency: "evt-123"},
      {name: "sendWebhook", idempotency: "web-456"}
    ]
  }]
})
